# Log File Genius - Git Attributes
# Ensures consistent line endings across platforms

# Force LF line endings for all shell scripts (critical for Mac/Linux compatibility)
*.sh text eol=lf

# Let Git handle line endings automatically for other text files
* text=auto

# Explicitly set line endings for specific file types
*.md text

# AGENTS.md is generated with an LF-only contract enforced by lfg generate
# and asserted by the smoke tests. Force LF in working copies on Windows too
# — otherwise autocrlf converts to CRLF on checkout and `git status` shows
# the file as modified after every clone.
product/AGENTS.md text eol=lf
*.yml text
*.yaml text
*.json text
*.xml text

# PowerShell scripts should use CRLF on Windows (Git will handle this with text=auto)
*.ps1 text

# Binary files
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary

